    "status": "present",
    "value": "Read the formula backwards. Scanning from the right means a count is seen before the element or group it applies to, so it can be held as a pending number. A closing parenthesis (seen first when going right to left) opens a group: push the current multiplier times the pending count. An opening parenthesis closes the group: pop. An element name adds pending times the top multiplier to that element's total. One pass computes every total without building a tree, and a final sort produces the output."
  },
